 r←SplitProjectUrl url;parts;host;owner;repo
⍝ Takes a project URL and returns a three-item vector: `(owner repo problem)`.\\
⍝ `problem` is empty when owner and repo could be established. Otherwise it says what
⍝ is wrong with the URL, and both owner and repo are empty.\\
⍝ It is safe to assume that the project lives on GitHub, but not that the URL says so
⍝ in the expected way, therefore:
⍝ * A protocol is optional, and "www." is ignored
⍝ * Anything below the repository ("/blob/main/README.md") is ignored
⍝ * A trailing ".git" is removed
⍝ * A host other than GitHub is refused rather than taken apart regardless
 r←'' ''('There is no project URL')
 :If 0<≢url
     parts←'/'(≠⊆⊢)url
     :If (⊂⎕C⊃parts)∊'http:' 'https:'
         parts←1↓parts
     :EndIf
     :If 0=≢parts
         r←'' ''('The project URL holds nothing but a protocol: ',url)
     :Else
         host←⎕C⊃parts
         :If 'www.'≡4↑host
             host←4↓host
         :EndIf
         :If 'github.com'≢host
             r←'' ''('The project does not live on GitHub but on <',(⊃parts),'>')
         :ElseIf 3>≢parts
             r←'' ''('The project URL carries no repository: ',url)
         :Else
             (owner repo)←parts[2 3]
             :If '.git'≡⎕C ¯4↑repo
                 repo←¯4↓repo
             :EndIf
             r←owner repo ''
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
